# Step 0.1.2 evidence — GCC 13.x apt version pin
# Date: 2026-06-11 (UTC). Image built from the digest-pinned base (see IMAGE_DIGEST).

## 1. Version discovery (inside pinned base, before any change)
$ podman run --rm <pinned-base-digest> bash -c 'apt-get update -qq && apt-cache policy gcc-13 gcc cpp-13 libgcc-13-dev'
  gcc-13        Candidate: 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1
  gcc (meta)    Candidate: 4:13.2.0-7ubuntu1
  cpp-13        Candidate: 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1
  libgcc-13-dev Candidate: 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1

## 2. Pin mechanism
- /etc/apt/preferences.d/motifbo-gcc13 (COPY of data/env/apt-pin-gcc13.pref), priority 1001,
  scope = src:gcc-13 binaries + meta gcc. Runtime libs (libasan8/libgcc-s1/...) deliberately
  NOT pinned: in noble they build from src:gcc-14 (see pref header); they are recorded and
  asserted instead.
- Explicit =version on apt-get install (fail-loud if the archive drops the version).

## 3. First build attempt — defect caught by smoke compile, fixed within the step
Build 52d141547eb6... compiled gcc-13 fine but `gcc -O2 -ffp-contract=off hello.c` failed:
  fatal error: stdio.h: No such file or directory
Trace: dpkg-query showed libc6-dev ABSENT — gcc-13 only Recommends libc6-dev and the
install uses --no-install-recommends. Fix: explicit pinned libc6-dev=2.39-0ubuntu8.7
added to the Containerfile install list. (Within-step implementation fix, not a project
red gate: no committed gate/test went red; cause fully traced before the fix.)

## 4. Final build
$ podman build --timestamp 0 -t localhost/motifbo-env:phase0 -f Containerfile .
  -> image id sha256:baccc2821580bb350a3491b5b76a5aec2f15ea33dc5af336c9d09ab7099de799

## 5. In-image verification
gcc -v  -> "gcc version 13.3.0 (Ubuntu 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1)"  [bytes: data/env/GCC_V_OUTPUT.txt]
gcc -dumpfullversion -> 13.3.0
dpkg-query (all 12 toolchain packages) -> exactly the versions in TOOLCHAIN.lock
Smoke compile: gcc -O2 -ffp-contract=off /tmp/hello.c -> prints 4.25 -> SMOKE_PASS
(-ffp-contract passed explicitly per the standing rule, CLAUDE.md / roadmap §3.2.)

## 6. CI assertion (scripts/check_toolchain.sh)
$ ./scripts/check_toolchain.sh
  TOOLCHAIN CHECK: PASS (13 assertions, zero diff)
Negative test (non-vacuity per §6.3): perturbed lock copy (gcc-13=13.2.0-WRONG) ->
  MISMATCH: lock has 'gcc-13=13.2.0-WRONG'; image has 'gcc-13=13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1'
  TOOLCHAIN CHECK: FAIL, exit=1
Re-run with real lock -> PASS.

RESULT: PASS — GCC 13.3.0 pinned (apt preferences + explicit versions), recorded, and
asserted with a proven-non-vacuous check.
